Satochip protocol implementation

This TypeScript module adapts protocol framing, command construction, parsing,
and secure-channel wire behavior from Satochip-Java:
https://github.com/Toporin/Satochip-Java
Revision ad297f14d1dbc0bb6f09e6ba17ca468f945d2a62 (Apache License, Version 2.0).

Upstream author attribution: Satochip Development Team / Toporin.
The complete Apache license is included alongside this file as
satochipProtocol.LICENSE and applies to this adapted module.

This version changes the implementation language, uses the wallet's existing
noble cryptographic primitives and WebCrypto AES-CBC, adds strict response bounds,
does not cache or retry PINs, and invalidates failed or stale operations.

It includes no source from the separately published SatochipSwift project.
Recovered response keys and wallet-key binding do not constitute manufacturer
attestation. The applet's secure response format has no response MAC; returned
signatures are checked against the expected wallet or Taproot output key.
